{"id": "EUVD-2026-106913", "enisaUuid": "0465e1e1-3bc4-38a4-99ec-7fa80b22292a", "description": "Astral uv before 0.11.6 contains a path traversal vulnerability that allows attackers to delete arbitrary files by supplying wheels with relative traversal paths in RECORD entries. Attackers can craft a malicious wheel whose RECORD references files outside the installation prefix, causing uv to delete those files when the user uninstalls the package.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T00:37:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T15:49:26", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/security/advisories/GHSA-pjjw-68hj-v9mw", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/astral-uv-before-0.11.6-arbitrary-file-deletion-via-wheel-record-entries"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-114110", "GHSA-m3wx-qqmx-qxvf"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.27, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "fd900f73-3c27-3b4a-b21a-70e5d91c5afa", "product": {"name": "uv", "vendor": {"name": "astral-sh"}}, "product_version": "0 <0.11.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "17659090-ee46-33ba-911f-5bd149f5ed1d", "vendor": {"name": "astral-sh"}}], "isExploited": false}